d2b0fe14e31b91b6,2026-11-03T18:00:05+00:00,meeting,upcoming,El Dorado County,Legistar,El Dorado County,,Zoning Administrator,2026-11-04,Attachment: C - Staff Presentation,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/289a0c48-fcf0-4151-85cc-35191bc304ca.pdf,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/289a0c48-fcf0-4151-85cc-35191bc304ca.pdf#page=2,2,false,0,parking,2,Transportation,outside,Agenda item,Agenda item,Project Description 2 A Minor Use Permit to allow for as-built barbed wire fencing; as- built fencing and retaining wall that exceeds seven (7) feet but is no more than 12 feet in height along the…,2,true,"...e; 55 as-built Recreational Vehicle (RV) carports within an existing self-storage operation; an as-built storage shed (8 foot x 16 foot); and expansion of RV parking onto the approximately two (2)-acre graded portion to the north, with 51 new RV carports and 29 new uncovered RV parking spaces. 26-1690 C 2 of 12",2,false,"[{""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Project Description 2 A Minor Use Permit to allow for as-built barbed wire fencing; as- built fencing and retaining wall that exceeds seven (7) feet but is no more than 12 feet in height along the…"", ""pages"": [2], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": false}]","[{""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 2, ""text"": ""...e; 55 as-built Recreational Vehicle (RV) carports within an existing self-storage operation; an as-built storage shed (8 foot x 16 foot); and expansion of RV parking onto the approximately two (2)-acre graded portion to the north, with 51 new RV carports and 29 new uncovered RV parking spaces. 26-1690 C 2 of 12""}]"
ff03f9dcef396b35,2026-11-03T18:00:05+00:00,meeting,upcoming,El Dorado County,Legistar,El Dorado County,,Zoning Administrator,2026-11-04,Attachment: A - Staff Report,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/b6199a6f-aac9-44a7-9455-28c41af508fb.pdf,https://eldorado.legistar1.com/eldorado/attachments/b6199a6f-aac9-44a7-9455-28c41af508fb.pdf#page=19,19,false,0,sidewalk; parking; scenic; stormwater; water quality,50,Transportation; Permitting; Science and Data,outside,Staff report,Staff report,COUNTY OF EL DORADO,"1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 12, 13, 16, 18, 19, 20, 22, 27, 28",true,"...uses are withi n a light industrial park. It appears that other vehicle storage uses in the business park also use barbed wire perimeter fencing. There is no sidewalk adjacent to the subject site, so this site is primarily accessible through vehicle access; it would not pose any issue to pedestrians. The project is consist...",19,false,"[{""type"": ""Staff report"", ""title"": ""COUNTY OF EL DORADO"", ""pages"": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 12, 13, 16, 18, 19, 20, 22, 27, 28], ""count"": 50, ""in_title"": false}]","[{""term"": ""sidewalk"", ""page"": 19, ""text"": ""...uses are withi n a light industrial park. It appears that other vehicle storage uses in the business park also use barbed wire perimeter fencing. There is no sidewalk adjacent to the subject site, so this site is primarily accessible through vehicle access; it would not pose any issue to pedestrians. The project is consist...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 1, ""text"": ""...l Vehicle (RV) carports and an existing 128-square-foot storage shed; 2. Proposed RV storage expansion consisting of 51 new RV carports and 29 new uncovered RV parking spaces; 3. As-built barbed wire fencing; 4. As-built fencing that exceeds seven (7) feet; and 5. Alternative Landscaping Plan Request. LOCATION: Northwest corn...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 2, ""text"": ""...Region. The entire site is graded and contains four (4) to six (6) inches of Aggregate Base (AB) gravel. RV operations, including RV carports and uncovered RV parking spaces, exist in the 6.13-acre southern portion of the parcel. The site contains perimeter fencing along most of the site boundar ies. Fencing consists of a...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 3, ""text"": ""...e interior northeastern side property line; 55 as-built carports totaling 20,880 square feet (sf); 51 new carports totaling 18,660 sf; and 29 new uncovered RV parking spaces, along with a small 128-square-foot as-built storage shed (8-foot by 16-foot) and associated site improvements, such as lighting and a request for an...""}, {""term"": ""scenic"", ""page"": 9, ""text"": ""...unusual circumstances. There are no unusual circumstances at the location of this proposed project; therefore, this exception does not apply. Exception (d) Scenic Highways. A categorical exemption shall not be used for a project which may result in damage to scenic resources, including but not limited to, trees, histor...""}, {""term"": ""scenic"", ""page"": 9, ""text"": ""...esources, including but not limited to, trees, historic buildings, rock outcroppings, or similar resources, within a highway officially designated as a state scenic highway. This does not apply to improvements which are required as mitigation by an adopted negative declaration or certified Environmental Impact Report (EI...""}, {""term"": ""scenic"", ""page"": 9, ""text"": ""...ents which are required as mitigation by an adopted negative declaration or certified Environmental Impact Report (EIR). The proposed project is not within a scenic highway corridor; therefore, this exception does not apply 26-1690 A 9 of 28""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 6, ""text"": ""..., County, and state agencies for review and comment. Comments were received from the El Dorado County Department of Transportation (DOT), Surveyor’s Office , Stormwater Division, and Air Quality Management District (AQMD) and have been incorporated as Conditions of Approval, as applicable. ENVIRONMENTAL REVIEW: The project...""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...waters (Central Valley RWQCB 2019). Discretionary projects must comply with the County’s West Slope Development and Redevelopment Standards (EDC 2024c), the Stormwater Management Plan (SWMP) for Western El Dorado County (EDC 2004b), and the County’s Grading, Erosion, and Sediment Control Ordinance (EDC 2013). Any future dev...""}, {""term"": ""stormwater"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...disturbance area of more than one ( 1) acre (43,560 square feet) would also be required to obtain coverage under the NPDES General Permit for Discharges of Stormwater Associated with Construction Activity (Construction General Permit Order 2022-0057- DWQ). Through compliance with all applicable regulations and requirements...""}, {""term"": ""water quality"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...ts, and preserve natural resources such as wetlands and riparian areas. Rationale: The project site is under the jurisdiction of the Central Valley Regional Water Quality Control Board ( RWQCB). The Central Valley RWQCB adopted the Water Quality Control Plan for the Sacramento and San Joaquin River Basins (Basin Plan) in 1975,...""}, {""term"": ""water quality"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...19, as amended in 2020. The purpose of the Basin Plan is to designate beneficial uses of waters within the Sacramento and San Joaquin River basins, establish water quality objectives to protect those beneficial uses, and implement a program needed to achieve those objectives. The Basin Plan establishes water quality standards f...""}, {""term"": ""water quality"", ""page"": 12, ""text"": ""...2022-0057- DWQ). Through compliance with all applicable regulations and requirements, potential future development at the project site would not violate any water quality standards or wast e discharge requirements or otherwise substantially degrade surface or groundwater quality. 26-1690 A 12 of 28""}]"
