) Occupancy Limits. An occupancy limit shall be established for each short-term rental based on individual characteristics of the dwelling unit and property. Overall maximum occupancy of an STR will be determined by the Planning and Building Divi...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 1, ""text"": ""...comdev APPEAL OF DECISION CASE NUMBER: WSTR24-0101 (STR Appeal – 801 Northwood Blvd. #31) BRIEF SUMMARY OF REQUEST: Appeal of a reduction in occupancy and parking for STR Permit WSTR24- 0101 STAFF PLANNER: Courtney Weiche, Senior Planner Phone Number: 775-328-3608 Email: CWeiche@washoecounty.gov CASE DESCRIPTION For...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 1, ""text"": ""...ffirm, modify, reverse, or remand the decision of the Director of Planning and Building reducing STR occupancy from eight (8) persons to four (4) persons and parking from two (2) spaces to one (1) space. The appellant requests reinstatement of eight-person occupancy. This appeal is submitted by Kristen O’Donnell , on behalf...""}, {""term"": ""parking"", ""page"": 2, ""text"": ""...m the decision of the Washoe County Direct or of Planning and Building limiting the STR at 801 Northwood Boulevard, Unit 31 to four (4) occupants and one (1) parking space. (Possible Motion on Page 7) Staff Report Contents Summary ..............................................................................................""}]"
