3a38a406e63a4a26,2026-11-03T18:00:05+00:00,meeting,past,Douglas County,Granicus,Douglas County,,Board of County Commissioners,2026-10-15,Agenda packet,https://d3n9y02raazwpg.cloudfront.net/douglascountynv/fd012da5-c4da-11f0-a7da-005056a89546-4b50c5b5-ef67-4e80-82ac-7b28f0e57fa1-1791584256.pdf,https://d3n9y02raazwpg.cloudfront.net/douglascountynv/fd012da5-c4da-11f0-a7da-005056a89546-4b50c5b5-ef67-4e80-82ac-7b28f0e57fa1-1791584256.pdf#page=10,10,false,158,,0,,agenda,Agenda item,Agenda item; Attachment,"Ellie Waller speaks: Good morning. I won't be here this afternoon. Sadly, there is no definition for glamping in the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency or Douglas County C odes. But with that said,…",10,true,"...Commissioners. Public Comment is open. Ellie Waller speaks: Good morning. I won't be here this afternoon. Sadly, there is no definition for glamping in the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency or Douglas County C odes. But with that said, Douglas County does have discretionary approval and interpretation rights at Design Review and building permits...",10,false,"[{""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ellie Waller speaks: Good morning. I won't be here this afternoon. Sadly, there is no definition for glamping in the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency or Douglas County C odes. But with that said,…"", ""pages"": [10], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""TRPA Advisory, Planning Commissioner at Large , and Community Development r epresentative for possible action before you. T hus allowing an enabling Commissioner R ice and future D istrict 4…"", ""pages"": [11], ""count"": 4, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Planning Agency also must make findings that the project complies with the required provisions of the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency code. These findings, under the TRPA code address what the project…"", ""pages"": [37], ""count"": 7, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. O’Hearn speaks: The public meeting before the TRPA Governing Board was September 24th of 2025. Chairman Gardner speaks: Thank you. Mr. O’Hearn speaks: Because the project was approved by the…"", ""pages"": [37], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. O’Hearn speaks: Because the project was approved by the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency, it moved to Douglas County for Design Review and approval. On April 27 th of 2026, the Planning Department…"", ""pages"": [37], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chapter 700 Section 030(b) regarding Land Use Regulations in the Tahoe Basin, it states that the County's role is, “performing Design Review and building inspection in the Basin.” The code section…"", ""pages"": [38], ""count"": 7, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""So we are in zoning area , so this is a recreational zoning area, i t's S-070B. Douglas County has adopted the Plan Area Statements from the TRPA. That being said, all of the zoning requirements are…"", ""pages"": [41], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Doherty speaks: I understand what you're saying, yeah. I'll just read you TRPA’s definition of a developed campground; I don't know that this is going to help . But, it says land or premises…"", ""pages"": [44], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: That's TRPA, but I'm asking the Douglas County Code . There’s a Douglas County Code, I just want to know if what she's saying is accurate because I haven't heard that…"", ""pages"": [44], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Vanillo speaks: Just to just to correct that , so Douglas County adopts the TRPA ’s use definitions. So we would have to pull it from the TRPA use definition. But yes, under the TRPA, cabin falls…"", ""pages"": [44], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Ritchie speaks: Chairman, if I may add something real quick ? Just for clarification, legal counsel has stated that TRPA has made this designation and it's their code that we're both referring…"", ""pages"": [44], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Ritchie speaks: So TRPA has made that designation or made that determination based on their own rules. I would say, though, these are great questions, and I would suggest that we allow appellant…"", ""pages"": [45], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Ritchie speaks: Having said that, since you've waded into this issue regarding TRPA, TRPA’s rules, the TRPA has made a determination that this is consistent. Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: I…"", ""pages"": [45], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: I didn't know the TRPA was our Supreme Court, that's what they taught us. That's what they taught us in law school, they may not be right, but they're final. Mr.…"", ""pages"": [45], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Hales speaks: To risk further muddying the waters and complicating matters, if this two story dome structure was not part of the information provided to TRPA, then recourse would be back…"", ""pages"": [45], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Vanillo speaks: And I would agree with you that if the scope of the project has now exceeded what was originally permitted by TRPA, it would have to go back to TRPA for re-approval and then back…"", ""pages"": [45], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chairman Gardner speaks: I appreciate you saying that because what we're looking here is you're going through the Design Review again. And that's not within our jurisdiction, in my views. That is…"", ""pages"": [47], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: Can I ask that question then? Just so we know for clarity, what would be the process if we say what they brought at plans time for a building permit, and you say, w hoa,…"", ""pages"": [47], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Doherty speaks: Thank you, good question. Yes, we would stop our review , we would tell them to go back to TRPA for approval. And then depending what the changes are, could be a M ajor or M inor…"", ""pages"": [48], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Vice Chairman Tolbert speaks: No, but going back to if we kicked it back to TRPA is what I'm trying to say. How would that happen? Ms. Doherty speaks: We would tell them. We would have to put the…"", ""pages"": [48], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Hales speaks: Can I? Oh, you are, go ahead. I was just going to say I think that's a really good question. And we don't know, I don't know the answer. The question is how do you get TRPA…"", ""pages"": [48], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: Again, I'm going to come to your defense again because yeah sure, if you build a hotel, it's outside of it. But what if it's something that's in the middle, in a gray…"", ""pages"": [48], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: Okay. So final statement and I'll let it go because we need to get her going. Our legal counsel is telling us we can't rule based upon whether this is a campground or…"", ""pages"": [48], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""But TRPA hasn't seen the floor plans, elevations and all of the other stuff , so how do they make that determination after we've already approved this? Mr. Ritchie speaks: If I may, Chairman? Just…"", ""pages"": [49], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Vanillo speaks: That is accurate and that is within Douglas County's purview in the finding criteria to determine whether or not it's meeting, whether or not the actual plans that have been…"", ""pages"": [49], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Ritchie speaks: So to answer your question, Commissioner Tarkanian, today you don't need to get int o whether TRPA got it wrong when they said this is a developed campground is consistent because…"", ""pages"": [49], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Chairman Gardner speaks: But that argument should be made to TRPA, should it not? Not to necessarily us, but the TRPA is the authorizing agency, they're the ones that created the zoning. They're the…"", ""pages"": [49], ""count"": 2, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Ms. Vanillo speaks: It's a two step approval process. Douglas County is the one that's going to be issuing all of the permits , Douglas County has the Design Review finding requirements. So in either…"", ""pages"": [49], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Mr. Ritchie speaks: Well, that's what's happened. The Design Review that occurred at the County at the staff level, they found that, again, they referred to the TRPA findings. But the staff…"", ""pages"": [50], ""count"": 1, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Okay, so under the Douglas County table, eating and drinking places require a special TRPA permit, plus an additional Douglas County review. And the food and beverage retail sales are prohibited in…"", ""pages"": [54], ""count"": 3, ""in_title"": true}, {""type"": ""Agenda item"", ""title"": ""Commissioner Tarkanian speaks: So again, we're going back t